	},
	{
		"path": "/root/Codex/@HBoxContainer@292/@ScrollContainer@480/@VBoxContainer@481/@Label@499",
		"rect": "[P: (374.0, 1085.0), S: (888.0, 61.0)]",
		"text": "Divine Physician. A master doctor of Jiankang whose needles and medicines save lives. He cures Song Jiang's back sores and serves as Liangshan's army physician."
	},
	{
		"path": "/root/Codex/@ColorRect@500/@Panel@501/@VBoxContainer@502/@HBoxContainer@503/@Label@504",
		"rect": "[P: (626.8, 26.0), S: (574.0, 101.0)]",
		"text": "An Daoquan　〔Earthly Star of Spirit · Divine Physician〕"
	},
	{
		"path": "/root/Codex/@ColorRect@500/@Panel@501/@VBoxContainer@502/@HBoxContainer@503/@Button@505",
		"rect": "[P: (1204.8, 26.0), S: (45.0, 101.0)]",
		"text": "✕"
	},
	{
		"path": "/root/Codex/@ColorRect@500/@Panel@501/@VBoxContainer@502/@ScrollContainer@509/@Label@510",
		"rect": "[P: (626.8, 157.0), S: (623.0, 4357.0)]",
		"text": "An Daoquan, known as the Divine Physician, came from Jiankang Prefecture. He was versed in every branch of medicine, from acupuncture to drugs and mineral remedies. Difficult illnesses, severe disorders, abscesses and ulcers, internal injuries and ailments contracted from outside all yielded remarkable results under his care. Throughout the martial world he was therefore respectfully called the Divine Physician. His skill could stand beside that of the ancient masters Bian Que and Hua Tuo, whose hands restored the dying to health, and his reputation spread far and wide.\n\nAn Daoquan had originally been a respected doctor in Jiankang, running an apothecary and treating the sick. He had no connection with Liangshan Marsh until a grave illness struck Song Jiang. The Liangshan heroes had defeated Gaotangzhou and Huazhou and were gaining renown. After receiving heavenly books at the Temple of the Mystic Lady and leading an attack on Zengtou Market, Song Jiang was exhausted by campaigning. A malignant sore erupted on his back; the infection grew dangerous, his whole body became red and swollen, and he could take neither food nor water. His life was in peril, and the doctors in the stronghold could do nothing. Dai Zong, the Marvelous Traveler, anxiously sought renowned physicians without success. Then Zhang Shun, the White Streak in the Waves, recalled that his mother had once been cured by An Daoquan of Jiankang. Such a miraculous doctor, he said, could surely save Song Jiang. Delighted, the chieftains asked Dai Zong and Zhang Shun to travel overnight to Jiankang and respectfully invite him.\n\nThey found An Daoquan in Jiankang, but he was then deeply involved with a courtesan named Li Qiaonu. Absorbed in wine and pleasure, he refused to accompany Zhang Shun to Liangshan. Repeated pleas and promises of a handsome reward only brought excuses. While Zhang Shun struggled with this refusal, disaster struck. Li Qiaonu had another lover, Zhang Wang, a hanger-on maintained by the brothel keeper and a villain who murdered for money. One night Zhang Wang killed both Li Qiaonu and the madam and stole their valuables. Zhang Shun stumbled into the affair and nearly became entangled in the prosecution. In desperation he turned the situation to his advantage, writing on the wall in blood: “The murderer is An Daoquan.” This cut off the physician's retreat. Seeing the bloodstained accusation, An Daoquan knew that remaining in Jiankang would bring legal disaster. With no way out, he packed his belongings and fled that night to Liangshan with Zhang Shun and Dai Zong. The episode of Zhang Shun's night of turmoil in Jiankang and his trick to bring the Divine Physician to the mountain introduces An Daoquan and also reveals how far Liangshan would go to recruit talent.\n\nOn reaching Liangshan, An Daoquan immediately examined Song Jiang's sore. After carefully assessing it, he used acupuncture, external medicines and restorative decoctions. Over several days the swelling subsided, and in fewer than ten days Song Jiang recovered, regained his spirits and resumed military affairs. An Daoquan remained in the stronghold to treat the chieftains and soldiers for illnesses and battle wounds, with success wherever his care was needed. When the 108 heroes assembled and their ranks were fixed, he was assigned the Earthly Spirit Star and the fifty-sixth seat among the Earthly Fiends. He supervised the physicians practicing both internal medicine and surgery, becoming the army's chief doctor.\n\nAfter Song Jiang accepted the imperial amnesty, An Daoquan accompanied the army. During the northern campaign against Great Liao and the campaigns against Tian Hu and Wang Qing, sick and wounded soldiers depended on his treatment. He saved countless lives through his medical skill. His eventual fate, however, differed from that of most comrades. As the army prepared to march south against Fang La, the emperor fell mildly ill, and the court physicians could not cure him. Someone recommended An Daoquan's extraordinary abilities. An imperial decree retained him in the capital and appointed him to the Imperial Medical Academy to attend the sovereign. Thus, ordered to remain in the capital, he did not join Song Jiang's southern campaign against Fang La.\n\nLater generations have often remarked upon his good fortune. In the campaign against Fang La, seven or eight of every ten Liangshan heroes were killed or grievously lost, leaving a scene of terrible devastation. By remaining in the capital, An Daoquan escaped that catastrophe intact. Instead of returning wrapped in a horsehide shroud, he received a post at the Imperial Medical Academy, enjoyed his salary and died peacefully in the capital. He was one of the rare members of the 108 to preserve his life and live out his natural years. The healing skills that saved so many Liangshan brothers ultimately saved their owner as well. The name Divine Physician was deserved: his story began well and ended well."
	}
]